      "rev_n_1_938ad8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_938ad8_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_938ad8",
        "thought_text": "Dynamic Programming Approach: Use dynamic programming to count permutations of length n with runs of length at most k. Define dp[i][j] as the number of valid permutations of length i ending with a run of length j. Transition between states based on whether the new element extends an existing run or starts a new one.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794407625.771324
      },
      "rev_n_2_506032_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_506032_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_506032",
        "thought_text": "Inclusion-Exclusion Principle: Calculate the total number of permutations and subtract those with runs longer than k. This involves calculating permutations with at least one run longer than k, then adding back those with at least two runs longer than k, and so on, using inclusion-exclusion.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794407625.771344
      },
      "rev_n_3_624960_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_624960_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_624960",
        "thought_text": "Generating Functions: Use generating functions to model the problem. Construct a generating function that captures the constraints on runs and then extract the coefficient of x^n to find the number of valid permutations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794407625.7713542
      },
